# Environment / Procedural Generators

Whenever you create a script that generates an environment (terrain, props, rooms, vegetation, level layouts, etc.),
you MUST create a PAIR of files so the user can generate it from the Inspector without entering Play Mode:

| Purpose | Path |
|---|---|
| Runtime generator | `Assets/Scripts/{Feature}/{Name}Generator.cs` |
| Inspector editor | `Assets/Editor/{Feature}/{Name}GeneratorEditor.cs` |
| Optional settings asset | `Assets/Scripts/{Feature}/{Name}Settings.cs` (ScriptableObject), instances in `Assets/ScriptableObjects/{Feature}/` |

## Runtime generator rules
- `MonoBehaviour` with `[DisallowMultipleComponent]` and `[AddComponentMenu("MyGame/{Feature}/{Name} Generator")]`.
- Public `Generate()` and `Clear()` methods hold ALL generation logic. The editor script only calls them.
- Must work in Edit Mode: no coroutines, no `Update`, no reliance on `Application.isPlaying`, no `Start`/`Awake` side effects.
- No `using UnityEditor;` in this file (wrap in `#if UNITY_EDITOR` only if truly unavoidable).
- Config via `[SerializeField] private` fields with `[Header]`, `[Tooltip]`, `[Min]`/`[Range]`. No magic numbers.
- Deterministic: expose `int seed` and `bool randomizeSeed`. Use a local `System.Random(seed)`, not global `UnityEngine.Random` state.
- Idempotent: `Generate()` calls `Clear()` first. Running it twice must not duplicate anything.
- Safe clearing: put everything generated under ONE child container (const name `"[Generated]"`).
  `Clear()` removes only that container and never touches hand-placed objects.
- Destroy correctly: `DestroyImmediate` in Edit Mode, `Destroy` in Play Mode.
- Prefer instantiating existing prefabs / primitives. If you generate Meshes or Materials at edit time,
  mention in the summary that they live inside the scene unless saved as assets.
- Validate inputs (null prefabs, zero counts) with clear `Debug.LogWarning` messages that include the generator's name; never throw.

## Editor script rules
- `[CustomEditor(typeof({Name}Generator))]`, namespace `MyGame.{Feature}.Editor`.
- Draw the default inspector first, then buttons: **Generate**, **Clear**, and **Randomize Seed & Generate**.
- Support Undo: `Undo.IncrementCurrentGroup()`, `Undo.SetCurrentGroupName(...)`,
  `Undo.RegisterFullObjectHierarchyUndo(generator.gameObject, ...)` before changes.
- After changes: `EditorUtility.SetDirty(generator)` and `EditorSceneManager.MarkSceneDirty(generator.gameObject.scene)`.
- Disable buttons when required fields are missing (`EditorGUI.BeginDisabledGroup`).
- Ask for confirmation (`EditorUtility.DisplayDialog`) before Clear if the container has many children.
- For slow generation, show `EditorUtility.DisplayProgressBar` and ALWAYS clear it in a `finally` block.

## Template: runtime

```csharp
using System.Collections.Generic;
using UnityEngine;

namespace MyGame.Environment
{
    [DisallowMultipleComponent]
    [AddComponentMenu("MyGame/Environment/Example Generator")]
    public class ExampleGenerator : MonoBehaviour
    {
        public const string ContainerName = "[Generated]";

        [Header("Setup")]
        [SerializeField] private GameObject _prefab;
        [SerializeField, Min(1)] private int _count = 10;
        [SerializeField, Min(0.1f)] private float _radius = 10f;

        [Header("Randomness")]
        [SerializeField] private int _seed = 12345;
        [SerializeField] private bool _randomizeSeed;

        public bool CanGenerate => _prefab != null && _count > 0;
        public int Seed { get => _seed; set => _seed = value; }

        public void Generate()
        {
            if (!CanGenerate)
            {
                Debug.LogWarning($"[{nameof(ExampleGenerator)}] Missing prefab or count is 0.", this);
                return;
            }

            Clear();
            if (_randomizeSeed) _seed = System.Environment.TickCount;

            var rng = new System.Random(_seed);
            var container = new GameObject(ContainerName).transform;
            container.SetParent(transform, false);

            for (int i = 0; i < _count; i++)
            {
                float angle = (float)(rng.NextDouble() * Mathf.PI * 2f);
                float dist = (float)rng.NextDouble() * _radius;
                var pos = new Vector3(Mathf.Cos(angle) * dist, 0f, Mathf.Sin(angle) * dist);

                var instance = Instantiate(_prefab, container);
                instance.transform.localPosition = pos;
            }
        }

        public void Clear()
        {
            var container = transform.Find(ContainerName);
            if (container == null) return;

            if (Application.isPlaying) Destroy(container.gameObject);
            else DestroyImmediate(container.gameObject);
        }
    }
}
```

## Template: editor

```csharp
using UnityEditor;
using UnityEditor.SceneManagement;
using UnityEngine;

namespace MyGame.Environment.Editor
{
    [CustomEditor(typeof(ExampleGenerator))]
    public class ExampleGeneratorEditor : UnityEditor.Editor
    {
        public override void OnInspectorGUI()
        {
            DrawDefaultInspector();
            var generator = (ExampleGenerator)target;

            EditorGUILayout.Space();
            using (new EditorGUI.DisabledScope(!generator.CanGenerate))
            {
                if (GUILayout.Button("Generate", GUILayout.Height(28)))
                    Run(generator, "Generate Example", generator.Generate);

                if (GUILayout.Button("Randomize Seed & Generate"))
                    Run(generator, "Generate Example (Random Seed)", () =>
                    {
                        generator.Seed = System.Environment.TickCount;
                        generator.Generate();
                    });
            }

            if (GUILayout.Button("Clear"))
                Run(generator, "Clear Example", generator.Clear);
        }

        private static void Run(ExampleGenerator generator, string undoName, System.Action action)
        {
            Undo.IncrementCurrentGroup();
            Undo.SetCurrentGroupName(undoName);
            Undo.RegisterFullObjectHierarchyUndo(generator.gameObject, undoName);

            action();

            EditorUtility.SetDirty(generator);
            EditorSceneManager.MarkSceneDirty(generator.gameObject.scene);
        }
    }
}
```

## Done checklist for every generator
- [ ] Both files created in the correct folders
- [ ] Generate and Clear work without Play Mode
- [ ] Running Generate twice does not duplicate objects
- [ ] Summary lists the "Verify in Unity" steps: add component to a GameObject, assign fields, click Generate
